# Git Commit Rules

## Commit Message Format
- Use conventional commit messages
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Keep commits atomic and focused
- Use meaningful branch names
- Review code before merging

## Conventional Commits
```bash
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <description>

# Examples:
feat(pokemon): add Pokemon3DViewer component
fix(api): handle network errors in getPokemonDetails
docs(readme): update installation instructions
style(ui): improve PokemonCard hover effects
refactor(api): extract PokemonCache utility
test(pokemon): add unit tests for PokemonCard
chore(deps): update axios to v1.6.0
perf(api): implement caching for Pokemon data
ci(github): add automated testing workflow
```

## Commit Types
- **feat**: 새로운 기능 추가
- **fix**: 버그 수정
- **docs**: 문서 수정
- **style**: 코드 스타일 변경 (포맷팅, 세미콜론 등)
- **refactor**: 코드 리팩토링
- **test**: 테스트 코드 추가/수정
- **chore**: 빌드 프로세스, 도구, 라이브러리 변경
- **perf**: 성능 개선
- **ci**: CI/CD 설정 변경

## Scope Examples
- **pokemon**: 포켓몬 관련 기능
- **api**: API 관련 기능
- **ui**: UI 컴포넌트
- **theme**: 테마 관련 기능
- **quiz**: 퀴즈 게임 기능
- **3d**: 3D 관련 기능
- **storage**: 저장소 관련 기능
- **test**: 테스트 관련
- **deps**: 의존성 관련

## Good Commit Messages
```bash
# Good examples:
feat(pokemon): add Pokemon3DViewer with Three.js integration
fix(api): handle 404 errors in getPokemonDetails
docs(readme): add installation and usage instructions
style(ui): improve PokemonCard hover animations
refactor(api): extract PokemonCache utility class
test(pokemon): add unit tests for PokemonCard component
chore(deps): update Next.js to v15.3.5
perf(api): implement localStorage caching for Pokemon data
ci(github): add automated testing on pull requests
```

## Bad Commit Messages
```bash
# Bad examples:
fix: bug fix
update: updated code
WIP: working on feature
feat: add stuff
fix: it works now
refactor: code changes
```

## Branch Naming
```bash
# Format: <type>/<description>

# Examples:
feature/pokemon-3d-viewer
feature/quiz-game
feature/pokemon-favorites
bugfix/api-error-handling
bugfix/pokemon-card-hover
hotfix/critical-api-fix
refactor/pokemon-cache
chore/update-dependencies
docs/update-readme
test/add-unit-tests
```

## Commit Workflow
```bash
# 1. Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature/pokemon-3d-viewer

# 2. Make changes and stage them
git add src/entities/pokemon/ui/Pokemon3DViewer.tsx
git add src/entities/pokemon/ui/Pokemon3DViewer.stories.tsx

# 3. Commit with descriptive message
git commit -m "feat(pokemon): add Pokemon3DViewer with Three.js integration

- Add Pokemon3DViewer component using @react-three/fiber
- Implement 3D model loading and display
- Add Storybook stories for component documentation
- Include proper error handling and loading states"

# 4. Push to remote
git push origin feature/pokemon-3d-viewer

# 5. Create pull request
# 6. Review and merge
```

## Atomic Commits
```bash
# Good: Atomic commits
git commit -m "feat(pokemon): add PokemonCard component"
git commit -m "feat(pokemon): add PokemonCard hover effects"
git commit -m "feat(pokemon): add PokemonCard accessibility features"

# Bad: Large commit with multiple changes
git commit -m "feat(pokemon): add PokemonCard with hover effects and accessibility"
```

## Commit Message Body
```bash
# Good: Detailed commit message
feat(pokemon): add Pokemon3DViewer component

Add a new 3D viewer component for Pokemon using Three.js and React Three Fiber.
The component includes:
- 3D model loading and display
- Orbit controls for user interaction
- Loading states and error handling
- Responsive design
- Accessibility features

Closes #123
```

## Pre-commit Hooks
```json
// package.json
{
  "husky": {
    "hooks": {
      "pre-commit": "lint-staged",
      "commit-msg": "commitlint -E HUSKY_GIT_PARAMS"
    }
  },
  "lint-staged": {
    "*.{ts,tsx}": [
      "eslint --fix",
      "prettier --write"
    ],
    "*.{json,md}": [
      "prettier --write"
    ]
  }
}
```

## Commit Lint Configuration
```javascript
// commitlint.config.js
module.exports = {
  extends: ['@commitlint/config-conventional'],
  rules: {
    'type-enum': [
      2,
      'always',
      [
        'feat',
        'fix',
        'docs',
        'style',
        'refactor',
        'test',
        'chore',
        'perf',
        'ci'
      ]
    ],
    'scope-enum': [
      2,
      'always',
      [
        'pokemon',
        'api',
        'ui',
        'theme',
        'quiz',
        '3d',
        'storage',
        'test',
        'deps',
        'ci'
      ]
    ],
    'subject-case': [2, 'always', 'lower-case'],
    'subject-max-length': [2, 'always', 50],
    'body-max-line-length': [2, 'always', 72]
  }
};
```

## Pull Request Template
```markdown
## Description
Brief description of the changes made.

## Type of Change
- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)
- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)
- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)
- [ ] Documentation update
- [ ] Code refactoring
- [ ] Performance improvement
- [ ] Test addition/update

## Testing
- [ ] Unit tests pass
- [ ] Integration tests pass
- [ ] Manual testing completed
- [ ] Accessibility testing completed

## Checklist
- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines
- [ ] Self-review completed
- [ ] Code is properly commented
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No console.log statements left
- [ ] Error handling implemented
- [ ] Loading states implemented
```

## Avoid
- Don't commit broken code
- Don't use vague commit messages
- Don't commit large files
- Don't ignore .gitignore rules
- Don't commit sensitive information
- Don't squash commits without good reason
- Don't force push to main branch